WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.180
- So more evidence comes out
that former President Trump

00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:04.680
was indeed trying to pressure the DOJ

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:07.200
to overturn the 2020 election.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:09.730
Specifically, the Biden
administration has released notes

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:12.160
of a December 27th meeting
between former President Trump

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:14.900
and then acting Attorney
General Jeffrey Rosen,

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:17.230
as well as Assistant
Deputy Attorney General

00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:18.130
Richard Donoghue.

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:20.300
The notes, and this goes under the heading

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:22.030
of real lawyers take notes,

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:23.360
the notes indicate that Trump was going

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:24.250
through his whole litany

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:26.310
of insane election conspiracy theories.

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:28.450
To which, Rosen and Donoghue pushed back,

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:30.290
saying that they couldn't do the things

00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:31.890
that he wanted them to.

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:33.370
To which, former President Trump replied

00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:36.607
he didn't expect them to do
it, but he said specifically,

00:00:36.607 --> 00:00:38.250
"Just say that the election was corrupt,

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:40.730
and leave the rest to me
and the R congressmen."

00:00:40.730 --> 00:00:43.010
And we lawyers call that
a Zelensky maneuver.

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:45.120
Just announced that
there's an investigation

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:47.320
or things are corrupt without
any evidence whatsoever,

00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:49.790
and then hope you can make hay out of it.

00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:51.590
So maybe that's good for
your own personal purposes,

00:00:51.590 --> 00:00:53.090
but it's not good for the rule of law.

00:00:53.090 --> 00:00:55.413
So we'll see if this ends up in court.

